    "title": "transistor driver",
    "body": "Control a motor through a transistor so the GPIO supplies only base current.\n\nA 1 kΩ resistor limits GPIO base current. The emitter is the grounded end of the low-side switch.\n\nPlace the diode cathode toward 5 V and anode toward the collector. The DC teaching model does not simulate inductive turn-off spikes, but real motors need this protection.\n\nUse analogWrite on D9 with three values, allowing enough time to see each speed.",
